<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mark-antony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-30">30 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mark Antony wins a final cavalry battle against Octavian</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> won a final cavalry battle against Octavian at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, but his infantry was defeated, and the next day his fleet and troops began to desert. Antony and Cleopatra took their own lives after Octavian's renewed invasion in early August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mark-antony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-1">1 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Octavian takes Alexandria and Mark Antony takes his own life</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Octavian's army entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, defeated and deserted, killed himself. Cleopatra's suicide days later ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic dynasty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> became a Roman province.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-annexation-of-egypt">Roman annexation of Egypt</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman annexation of Egypt took place in 30 BCE, when Octavian took Alexandria after the defeat of Mark Antony and Cleopatra VII.</p></div></li></ol></section>
